# Temperance marker — cli#254 sub-steps 5+6 (Docker wire)
- date: 2026-09-27
- branch: feat/254-docker-wire
- ceremony-class: (c) cross-cutting wire (Dockerfile + entry.sh + smoke-report + runbook)
- prior: sub-step 4.5 shipped (PR #263 merged 35b79ef); Batches A/B/C
  shipped; walking-skeleton 3 drives real-body shipped.
- scope-decision:
  - right-thing: close the cli#254 chain by wiring interactive drives
    into the actual Docker CI run. Install expect in the container.
    Add a new V2 step to entry.sh that fires the 3 walking-skeleton
    drives. Extend smoke-report with interactive rows. Extend the
    docker-smoke runbook exit-code table.
  - right-way: fail-soft per Nygard — missing SMOKE_GH_TOKEN skips
    Class 3 skills (/promote, /build) with a WARN, not a hard fail.
    Missing expect binary means the whole V2 interactive step no-ops
    with a clear message. Adopters running against older cli versions
    (no smoke-drive-generic.sh) skip cleanly.
  - drift-trigger: any edit to smoke-expect verbs, walking-skeleton
    drives, Batch A/B/C entries, or sub-step 4.5 setup/teardown is
    drift. This scope wires existing pieces; it does not modify them.
- blast-radius:
  - inside scope: harness/docker/Dockerfile.cold-adopter (add expect),
    harness/docker/exit-codes.sh (add 30-34 for interactive class),
    harness/docker/entry.sh (add function + wire), scripts/smoke-report.sh
    (interactive rows), docs/runbook/docker-smoke.md (exit-code table).
  - outside scope: /release + /deploy drives; dummy-repo PAT setup
    (that's an adopter action, README calls it out); the generic
    driver body.
  - hard ceiling untouched: auth, schema, security.
- authorization: agent-merges-within-scope.
